BUG in closeout-lint.sh AND hygiene-lint.sh: PROJECT_REPO_PATH is read from schedule/*.conf with sed and $HOME is NEVER EXPANDED, so both guards report every registered repo as absent. Found 2026-08-05 from senechal. Repro: closeout-lint (no args) prints 'FLAG [missing-repo] senechal: $HOME/Documents/Projects/senechal does not exist' for all 13 projects while every one of those directories exists; hygiene-lint senechal prints '(no git repo at that path -- skipped)'. Site: realisateur/bin/closeout-lint.sh:147 (and the identical loop hygiene-lint.sh copies -- the comment says 'same loop as hygiene-lint.sh', so fix both) -- the sed captures the LITERAL string $HOME/... and line 186's [ -d "$repo" ] then always fails. Fix is one expansion at capture time (eval/parameter-substitution of a leading $HOME, or source the conf in a subshell as sync-crontab.sh already must). WHY THIS MATTERS MORE THAN A NORMAL BUG: this is the CLOSING guard, and it is null-discriminating in the silence-audit sense -- because every repo short-circuits at the -d test, the dirty-tree/unpushed-commits/no-upstream checks NEVER RUN FOR ANY REPO, and the output looks identical whether the ecosystem is pristine or every repo has unpushed work. It is loud (14 FLAGs) but it discriminates nothing, which is exactly the defect /cloture step 1 says is close to a verdict by construction. closeout-lint --repo <path> is unaffected (different code path, does not read the conf) and is the working route meanwhile. NOT FIXED BY SENECHAL: realisateur's domain, and check-project-busy realisateur reports BUSY (interactive session pid 219074, live since 2026-07-31).
